<title>USA: ConAgra to pay millions in grain probe - WSJ.</title>
<headline>ConAgra to pay millions in grain probe - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>ConAgra Inc has agreed to pay millions of dollars in penalties to settle an investigation over its Peavey Grain unit's practice of spraying water on stored grain, the Wall Street Journal reported Thursday.</p>
<p>The paper quoted people familiar with the probe as saying that the Justice Department is also seeking charges against some former Peavey employees.</p>
<p>The report said a company spokesperson declined comment, but quoted sources as saying that the penalties total less than $10 million.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
